# Evidence JSON must be byte-identical between the working tree and the committed blob,
# so a published file_sha256 verifies against `git cat-file blob`.
# Deterministic LF in both directions (overrides core.autocrlf on Windows).
# Cover EVERY evidence file this card publishes, not just JSON: a reviewer who
# re-checks-out the branch must get byte-identical files, or published file_sha256
# values stop verifying against the commit (the Round-1 defect class).
*.json text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
raw/*.json text eol=lf
